  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if the damage results from a sudden, accidental, and covered peril like a windstorm, hail, or a fallen tree branch.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if the damage results from a sudden, accidental, and covered peril like a windstorm, hail, or a fallen tree branch"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Storm Damage: Leaks caused by severe wind, heavy hail, lightning, or a tree crashing through the roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Interior Water Damage: Ruined drywall, flooring, or furniture caused by a sudden, covered roof failure are often paid for even if the old wear-and-tear on the roof itself is excluded."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Is Not Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wear and Tear: Leaks from an old, aging roof near the end of its lifespan."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Lack of Maintenance: Rot, neglected shingle decay, or slow leaks you failed to fix promptly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Seep Damage: Gradual water damage that happens over many months without a specific storm event."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Next Steps for a Leak"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stop the water: Catch drips in buckets and move valuables to prevent extra damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos: Photograph both the wet ceiling and the damaged roof area before making temporary fixes. Read guidance on Roof Leak Repair in Utah for safe containment tips.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Roof Leak Repair in Utah",
                "link": "https://skyridgeco.com/blog/roof-leak-repair-utah-2026"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check your policy: Look at your specific deductible and storm coverage limits."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What caused the leak (a recent storm or an old roof)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Where is the water coming in?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare for the next steps or find local inspection help."
